    "result_text": "All 284 tests pass, including the new `Cp17Tests`. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` rule for owner creation, following the existing pattern used by the other computed owner fields (`namesakeCount`, `membershipTier`, etc.).\n\n**What it does:** When creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`, `sharesHousehold` is set to `true` if another owner already has the same address and city, otherwise `false`. Creation is still allowed in both cases.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` \u2014 sets `sharesHousehold` before saving, via a new `sharesHousehold(Owner)` helper that scans existing owners for a matching address + city (case/whitespace-insensitive, reusing the existing `normalize` helper). Computed after `canonicalCity` so the city comparison uses the canonical spelling.\n- `Owner` model \u2014 added the `sharesHousehold` field (`@Column(name = \"shares_household\")`) with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it into `OwnerDto`.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `sharesHousehold` boolean (readOnly) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in the response.\n- Schema SQL (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `shares_household BOOLEAN` column to the `owners` table.",
